                        "entry_id": "bb2cc26e-41be-335f-8d33-044f374cb577",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A regular pattern of oligonucleotide sizes on electrophoretic gels, resulting from the fragmentation of DNA strands during cell death."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72244016-d06b-404d-a4a2-f9314ba8bc92",
                                "sense_id": "0b7133ff-939f-3f98-b285-a7e592c108ed",
                                "text": "For example, tobacco cell cultures grown at 5oC, resulted in a loss of viability relative to control cells and exhibited DNA laddering (Koukalova et al., 1997)."
